      "writtenOn": "2025-11-27T06:06:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Here is an updated direction based on the discussion.\nThe read behavior is selected using a build-time ELAN_READ_MODE defined in the sensor-specific config header. The PAL code simply dispatches to the appropriate read function:\nstatic int elan_read_fn(uint16_t *short_raw)\n{\n    switch (ELAN_READ_MODE) {\n    case IMAGE_READ_MODE:\n        return elan_image_read(short_raw);\n    case LINEWISE_READ_MODE:\n        return elan_image_read_linewise(short_raw);\n    default:\n        return -EINVAL;\n    }\n}\nThis keeps the logic build-time determined, avoids adding #ifdef to the PAL file, and keeps the configuration clean and centralized.\nIf this direction looks good, I can update the full CL accordingly.",
      "parentUuid": "b4983959_b8d15bc0",
      "revId": "d62e37bf63d6ef53461d08d1391b7a0d4c0c4623",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
