      "writtenOn": "2025-11-28T07:28:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "But switch statement is used for run-time, not for build-time. What you can do is you can define e.g. `IMAGE_READ_MODE` in the sensor specific header, as you mention and do the #ifdef tree in `elan_read_fn`. However I still think using Kconfigs is better and follows Zephyr style in a better way. IMO the best solution would be to define a [choice](https://docs.zephyrproject.org/latest/build/kconfig/setting.html#configuring-choices) config, something like `ELAN_READ_MODE`, add proper choices that are selected by sensor specific config.",
      "parentUuid": "0a4a0c5d_4f6dca5c",
